<title>USA: D.R. Horton backlog a record, sees record yr.</title>
<headline>D.R. Horton backlog a record, sees record yr.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Texas 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>D.R. Horton Inc said Wednesday its sales backlog on June 30 rose 38 percent to 1,977 homes or $343.7 million, the highest quarter-end level in its history.</p>
<p>D.R. Horton, which announced third quarter results today, said it expects earnings for fiscal 1997 will also rank as a company record.</p>
<p>The company posted net income for its third quarter ended June 30, 1997 of $9.8 million, or $0.26 per share, up from $7.4 million or $0.23 per share a year ago.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
